WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.252
Sanuuu!

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:04.421
- You’re probably the best receiver
in the game in Throw Power.

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:05.171
- Thank you.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:08.174
- But if you can throw it 70, then
your rating’s gonna keep goin’ up.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.010
- What happens if he throws it 45?

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.136
- It could go down.

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:12.137
- There’s risk here.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.764
♪♪♪

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:18.268
What’s going on, everybody?

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:20.979
Lefkoe here in Atlanta to
meet up with Mohamed Sanu,

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:23.773
the wide receiver with the
strongest arm in the NFL.

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:29.320
I wanna know how many quarterbacks
he can throw it farther than.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.114
And just like a good State Farm agent,

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:33.575
Mohamed Sanu is just lookin’
to help us out.

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:36.453
See, I’m the sultan of segues, 
and that’s called “branded content.”

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.872
It’s a little bit of a reach. I apologize.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.541
But in all seriousness, State Farm is great.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.251
Mohamed Sanu can throw far.

00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:44.085
Let’s get it on.

00:00:48.923 --> 00:00:51.801
♪♪♪

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:55.138
- Yooo!

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.140
Sanuuu!

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:57.682
- What’s up?

00:00:57.682 --> 00:00:58.933
- What’s good, man?

00:00:58.933 --> 00:00:59.976
- How you doin’?

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:02.020
- Dude, I’m so excited
we’re about to do this.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:02.896
- Yeah, I’m pumped too.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.564
- We get to show off
that arm cannon of yours.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.523
- I’m pumped too, man.

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:06.649
- Lemme see.

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:08.068
- (Laughing)
- How much do you think we got in there?

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.319
75, 80?

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:10.695
- I don’t know, we gonna see.

00:01:10.695 --> 00:01:14.240
- So we have 10 of the top quarterbacks in
the NFL laid out on the field with their

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.617
longest throws.

00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:19.996
So we got Eli, Brady, Rodgers,
all the way up to Patrick Mahomes

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:20.997
at freakin’ 80 yards.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:24.375
How many of these guys do you think
you can throw it farther than?

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:26.252
You’ve seen guys on the sideline—

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.755
- Maybe, like—maybe,
like, 50 percent of them.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.381
40, 50 percent.
- OK.

00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:31.925
If you reach Rodgers—

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:32.425
- Yeah.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.843
- At 73?

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:35.220
Successful day.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:35.762
- Right.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.847
- I think you’re gonna pass Brady and Russ.

00:01:37.847 --> 00:01:38.348
- Right.

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:39.849
I mean, I think so too.

00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:40.558
Maybe.

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:42.102
- That throw that I saw on Twitter—

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:42.685
- Uh-huh.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:43.728
- In, like, the backyards?

00:01:43.728 --> 00:01:44.312
- Oh, yeah.

00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:47.065
- You were like, “How far is
that?!” How far was that, you think?

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.233
- It was pretty far.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:51.027
It was, like, it was definitely 60-plus.

00:01:51.027 --> 00:01:53.113
But I had to throw it over
the tree too, and a house.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.697
- That’s crazy!

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:57.617
I also wanna see how fast you can throw it.
- Mhmm.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.952
- We got a radar gun.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.120
- Radar gun it.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.287
- Have you ever done this before?

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.413
- Nah, I never done a radar gun.

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:04.999
- And I’m gonna try and catch one of your
passes, so please don’t break my fingers.

00:02:04.999 --> 00:02:06.251
- OK.

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:07.544
I’ve done that before.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:08.962
- You’ve broken someone’s finger?!
- Oh, definitely.

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:10.797
- Here we go, here we go.

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:14.467
Damn!

00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:16.553
54.

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:18.346
You know that’s higher
than most quarterbacks?

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:23.226
Oh my God, and I caught—no!

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:24.185
Dammit!

00:02:24.185 --> 00:02:26.104
I got so afraid, I wanted to talk to you.

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:27.063
What was that?

00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:27.814
- 54.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:28.815
- 54!

00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:30.900
I’m catchin’ the next one.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.860
Here we go.

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:35.864
Ohhh.

00:02:35.864 --> 00:02:36.990
- 56.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.449
- 56!

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.165
You were impressed by that catch though?

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.666
- Yeah, I was very impressed by the catch.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.709
- I was nervous.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:49.460
You played high school QB, right?
- Yeah.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.171
- That’s probably when the
arm was the most fluid?

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.172
- Oh, definitely.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.840
- How far are we throwin’ back then?

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.887
- Um, it was one day—it was a
little windy—I threw 84 and—

00:02:58.887 --> 00:02:59.846
- 84!

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.556
- Yeah, the one day it wasn’t
windy, it was completely—

00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:03.558
- What?! That’s, like, double me, bro.

00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:08.062
I can imagine you weren’t too thrilled
with the Madden ratings that came out.

00:03:08.062 --> 00:03:08.897
- No.

00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:11.941
- Throw Power went from a 78 to a 72.

00:03:11.941 --> 00:03:13.151
They made their ratings tougher—

00:03:13.151 --> 00:03:14.194
- Yeah, they did.
- Which I understand.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:14.903
- It’s cool.

00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:15.904
- But a 72.

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:17.280
- Yeah, that’s very, very—

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.281
- I mean, that’s—Eli’s higher than that.

00:03:19.407 --> 00:03:22.535
But now this is your chance to prove
everybody wrong, because we brought in a

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.079
Madden ratings adjustor.

00:03:25.079 --> 00:03:31.920
♪♪♪

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.756
That’s the guy that you need to impress—
- He’s gonna adjust it?

00:03:34.756 --> 00:03:36.299
- If you wanna get your numbers up.

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:37.217
- What’s up, guys?

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.092
- How you doin’,
nice to meet you.

00:03:38.092 --> 00:03:40.178
- Hey, I’m Clint Oldenburg, Madden
Ratings Performance Adjustor.

00:03:40.178 --> 00:03:40.762
- My man.

00:03:40.762 --> 00:03:44.098
- We have you at a 72 Throw Power,
which is pretty good for a receiver.

00:03:44.098 --> 00:03:46.142
You’re probably the best receiver
in the game in Throw Power.

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:47.060
- Thank you.
- Oooh.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.897
- But if you can throw it past some of those
guys, then your rating’s gonna keep going up.

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.815
- What happens if he throws it, like, 45?

00:03:52.815 --> 00:03:54.651
- Then the rating could go down.

00:03:54.651 --> 00:03:55.526
- It could go down?

00:03:55.526 --> 00:03:56.694
- It could go down.

00:03:56.694 --> 00:03:57.320
There’s risk here.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.114
- It’s time for Mohamed
Sanu to throw the ball deep.

00:04:06.537 --> 00:04:07.372
- (Offscreen) 67.

00:04:07.372 --> 00:04:08.581
67!

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:11.042
- All right, that’s,
that’s a good first throw.

00:04:11.042 --> 00:04:12.418
- What are we thinkin’ right away?

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.462
- I mean, it—
- Did that—was that impressive to you?

00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:15.463
- That was pretty impressive.

00:04:15.463 --> 00:04:18.341
I mean, he has a quarterback background.
I think he can go a little further.

00:04:18.341 --> 00:04:21.135
You know that you threw it past
Matt Ryan, your quarterback.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.680
- Yeah, I knew that.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.847
- He knew!

00:04:24.847 --> 00:04:26.015
- All right, Throw 2. Here we go.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.479
- That’s a spiral-and-a-half.

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:33.648
- He spun it.

00:04:33.648 --> 00:04:36.025
I think that’s right at 70.

00:04:36.025 --> 00:04:37.735
- Wow.
- It’s close.

00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:39.153
- 69.

00:04:39.153 --> 00:04:40.154
Nice.

00:04:40.154 --> 00:04:43.241
- I have a little pressure to add to this.
- OK.

00:04:43.241 --> 00:04:46.160
- If you can hit 70—which, you’re
really close, you’re a yard off—

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:46.744
- Mhmm.

00:04:46.744 --> 00:04:51.082
- We’re gonna add a package of plays to
the Falcons playbook with you aligned at quarterback.

00:04:51.082 --> 00:04:51.749
- OK.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:53.876
Just for that, I’mma get that for
the fans, just cuz you said that.

00:04:53.876 --> 00:04:55.003
- Oooh!
- All right.

00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:57.922
- Cuz, you know, I know they been
askin’ for it, tweets all the time.

00:04:57.922 --> 00:04:59.465
So just for that, I gotchu.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.509
- I don’t wanna add too much pressure.
- There ain’t no such thing as pressure.

00:05:01.509 --> 00:05:02.593
- A man of the people, Mohamed Sanu.

00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:05.638
- Listen, ain’t no such thing as pressure.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.848
- That extra yard—no such thing as pressure.

00:05:06.848 --> 00:05:08.391
- I just make stuff happen.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:13.896
(Grunting)
♪♪♪

00:05:24.365 --> 00:05:25.533
- (Offscreen) 71.5!

00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:26.492
- Yesss!

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.036
- For the fans, for the fans!
- Just for the fans.

00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:29.370
- Get up, get up, get up!

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.371
- Just for the fans!

00:05:30.371 --> 00:05:31.664
- Ahhh!

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:34.500
And he’s got a play in the
playbook as a quarterback!

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.251
- Just for the fans.

00:05:35.251 --> 00:05:36.252
- Yes!

00:05:36.252 --> 00:05:37.754
I was really nervous.

00:05:37.754 --> 00:05:39.172
I thought 69 was gonna be your top.

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:40.757
- Nahhh.
- 71—

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:42.508
- Once I felt it here, I knew I could do it.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.676
- Oooh, oooh.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.428
- That’s pretty good.

00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:47.764
- Sa-nuuu.

00:05:47.764 --> 00:05:50.099
- I think we’re definitely in the 80s now.

00:05:50.099 --> 00:05:51.684
You came in with a 72 Throw Power.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.770
I think we’re definitely in the 80s.
- Definitely in the 80s?

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.063
- This is the best thing ever.

00:05:55.063 --> 00:05:56.606
I feel like I’ve given a gift.

00:05:56.606 --> 00:05:58.941
I didn’t even know I was doin’ all this.
- You givin’ a gift for all the fans.

00:05:58.941 --> 00:06:01.736
- I can’t stop high-fivin’ you for no reason.
- You gave a gift to the Falcons fans.

00:06:01.736 --> 00:06:03.363
- Yeah, Falcons fans get to use you.
- Yeah, we gave a gift to all the fans.

00:06:07.742 --> 00:06:09.619
- (Brandon Gaudin) So barely
time to catch our breath.

00:06:09.619 --> 00:06:12.538
Here’s 1st-and-10 just outside the red zone.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:15.708
Lookin’ to throw, Mohamed Sanu!

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.544
Got his star receiver, it’s Jones!

00:06:24.675 --> 00:06:28.846
- So we were hopin’ Mohamed Sanu
would outthrow 16 NFL quarterbacks.

00:06:28.846 --> 00:06:34.894
At 71.5, he outthrew 28 starting
quarterbacks in the NFL.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:39.524
We improved his Throw Power rating, and it
makes me think: NFL GMs, instead of looking

00:06:39.524 --> 00:06:42.652
for a quarterback, maybe you
should look for a wide receiver.

00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:44.821
Or at least pick him up in Madden.

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:51.953
What's up, guys?
It's Derrius Guice of the Washington Redskins.

00:06:51.953 --> 00:06:53.830
Make sure you subscribe to Bleacher Report

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:57.542
to catch more episodes from
Ditch the Playbook with Lefkoe.

00:06:57.542 --> 00:06:58.709
Sadly.

00:06:58.709 --> 00:07:00.670
[Laughing]
- [Offscreen] That was great.

